Reason: whenever a tile comes or goes the GMS1 draw list's tile run (patch 0064) is rebuilt, and it was sorted with
qsort and the general drawable comparison: ~58,000 comparisons for rm_a3h04's ~4,800 tiles, on most frames while its
sand crumbles. Tiles sort by depth, higher first, then by their place in the room's array, so a bucket per depth,
filled in array order, gives exactly that order without comparing two tiles. A room with more than 64 tile depths
keeps qsort.
Upstream: Speed only, every platform. Retires this patch when merged.

